item.description:
*Originally posted on Facebook, April 20, 2022*
"We cannot be ready to meet the Lord by waking when the cry is heard, "Behold, the Bridegroom!" and then gathering up our empty lamps to have them replenished. We cannot keep Christ apart from our lives here, and yet be fitted for His companionship in heaven.
In the parable the wise virgins had oil in their vessels with their lamps. Their light burned with undimmed flame through the night of watching. It helped to swell the illumination for the bridegroom's honor. Shining out in the darkness, it helped to illuminate the way to the home of the bridegroom, to the marriage feast." {Christ's Object Lessons ch.29 p.414; Ellen G. White}

*Originally posted on Facebook, July 30, 2022*

Acts 13:40  Beware therefore, lest that come upon you, which is spoken of in the prophets; 
13:41  Behold, ye despisers, and wonder, and perish: for I work a work in your days, a work which ye shall in no wise believe, though a man declare it unto you.

*Originally posted on Facebook, October 15, 2022*
From a bacteria to a cell; from a chicken to a camel no human has ever created any living thing, and no one ever will. Let every atom of pride be putrefied. "Not all the wisdom and skill of man can produce life in the smallest object in nature. It is only through the life which God Himself has imparted, that either plant or animal can live. So it is only through the life from God that spiritual life is begotten in the hearts of men. Unless a man is "born from above," he cannot become a partaker of the life which Christ came to give. John 3:3, margin." {SC 67.2}
